# Chicken Pozole Verde

## Recipe Name: Chicken Pozole Verde

## Servings: 6 to 8

## Prep Time: 45 mins (active)

## Cook Time: 30 mins (about 1 hr 15 mins start to finish)

## Ingredients:
### Soup:
- 7 cups chicken stock or low-sodium broth
- 2 cups water
- 4 chicken breast halves, bone-in and skin-on
- 1 pound tomatillos, husked and halved
- 1 small onion, quartered
- 2 poblano chiles, cored, seeded, and quartered
- 2 jalapeños, seeded and quartered
- 4 large garlic cloves, smashed
- 1/2 cup cilantro, chopped
- 1 tablespoon oregano leaves (Mexican oregano if you have it)
- 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt, plus more to taste
- 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper, plus more to taste
- 1 tablespoon vegetable oil
- 3 (15-ounce) cans hominy, drained

### Toppings:
- Iceberg lettuce, finely shredded
- Radishes, sliced
- Onion, chopped
- Avocado, diced
- Sour cream
- Tortilla chips
- Lime wedges

## Instructions:
### Poach the Chicken:
1. Bring the chicken stock and water to a boil in a large enameled cast-iron casserole or Dutch oven.
2. Add the chicken breasts skin side down. Cover and simmer over very low heat until they are tender and cooked through, about 25 minutes.
3. Skim the fat off the cooking liquid and throw it out. Leave the liquid in the pot.
4. Move the chicken to a cutting board or plate. When it is cool enough to handle, shred the meat. Throw out the bones and skin.

### Make the Green Sauce:
1. Put the tomatillos, onion, poblanos, jalapeños, garlic, cilantro and oregano in a blender. Pulse until coarsely chopped, scraping down the sides.
2. Run the blender and pour in 1 cup of the cooking liquid. Puree until smooth. Season with salt and pepper.
3. Heat the oil in a large deep skillet until it shimmers. Add the tomatillo puree and cook over moderate heat, stirring now and then, until the sauce turns a deep green. About 12 minutes. Do not rush this step.

### Finish and Serve:
1. Pour the green sauce into the cooking liquid in the casserole. Add the hominy. Bring to a simmer over moderate heat.
2. Add the shredded chicken. Season with salt and pepper. Cook just until it is heated through.
3. Ladle it into deep bowls. Pass the lettuce, radishes, onion, avocado, sour cream, tortilla chips and lime wedges at the table.

## Notes:
- Hominy is the whole point of the dish. Do not swap it for regular corn.
- Use bone-in, skin-on chicken breast halves. Poaching them on the bone keeps the meat moist. Boneless breast dries out here.
- Use Mexican oregano if you can find it. It has citrus notes that sit better with the tomatillos than Mediterranean oregano does.
- Do not skip the skimming. The Food & Wine test kitchen says it fixes the flavor, the texture and the look of the soup.
- Cook the green sauce down for the full 12 minutes. This takes the raw edge off the tomatillos and mellows the chiles.
- Make ahead: cook as far as the poached chicken and the skimmed liquid. Cool it, cover it and put it in the fridge overnight. Make the sauce and finish the pot the next day.
- Prep more toppings than you think you need. People go back for more as they eat.
- The source spells the dish "Posole Verde". Food & Wine also uses "posole" throughout. Same dish.
- Source: Food & Wine, "Chicken Posole Verde" by Anya von Bremzen. https://www.foodandwine.com/chicken-pozole-verde-6413925

